&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Associate Director, Reliability (MRE)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Associate Director, Reliability (MRE), you will oversee the team of reliability engineers, the reliability planner/scheduler, CMMS systems, Quality Engineering, and industrial SMEs in refrigeration, kitchen equipment, and other critical utilities. You&#39;ll also take direct ownership of&amp;nbsp;all life-cycle maintenance projects across US sites — including utility expansion/modification, new equipment installation (in coordination with engineering), and refrigeration system projects.&amp;nbsp;You&#39;ll lead hands-on, engaging, motivating, and coaching your team members directly.&amp;nbsp;Partnering with M&amp;amp;RE senior leadership, you&#39;ll define, develop, and deliver the facilities&amp;nbsp;maintenance roadmap and set the standard for operational efficiency at your fulfillment center.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;You will…&lt;br&gt;• Oversee MRE-related projects, including facilities maintenance across electrical,&amp;nbsp;refrigeration, building, and grounds&lt;br&gt;• Asset Performance: Implement Reliability-Centered Maintenance (RCM), root cause&amp;nbsp;analysis (RCA), and failure mode and effects analysis (FMEA) to reduce downtime.&lt;br&gt;• Motivate, engage, coach, and inspire a team of specialists — building a positive team&amp;nbsp;dynamic that encourages feedback and drives change from within&lt;br&gt;• Manage outside vendors and facilitate planned and unplanned Life cycle&amp;nbsp;repairs/replacements&lt;br&gt;• Ensure maintenance regulations are followed&lt;br&gt;• Maintain a current list of contractors to ensure emergency repairs are handled&amp;nbsp;promptly&lt;br&gt;• Identify problems and brainstorm improvement ideas for the fulfillment center/s&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;You are…&lt;br&gt;• Customer Centric: You&#39;re passionate about delivering on commitments to your&amp;nbsp;customers&lt;br&gt;• Bold: You have passion and grit; you&#39;re not afraid to give feedback to your team and&amp;nbsp;your manager&lt;br&gt;• Agile: You roll with the punches, adapt quickly to change, and deliver results in a&amp;nbsp;fast-paced, autonomous environment&lt;br&gt;• Decisive: You know when making a decision is as important as the time it takes to&amp;nbsp;make it&lt;br&gt;• Problem-solver: You know there&#39;s no one-size-fits-all approach; you think outside&amp;nbsp;the box and enjoy deep-diving issues to find solutions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;You have…&lt;br&gt;• 10+ years&#39; experience managing facilities maintenance/operations and reliability&amp;nbsp;within the Food/Beverage/Perishables/Distribution industry&lt;br&gt;• Bachelor&#39;s degree is preferred, in Mechanical, Electrical, or another related&amp;nbsp;engineering field&lt;br&gt;• Interested in spending most of your time on the shop floor, working directly with all&amp;nbsp;levels of staff&lt;br&gt;• High level of integrity and ethics with excellent follow-through&lt;br&gt;• Excitement for working in a start-up environment with high ambiguity and change&lt;br&gt;• Effective communication skills across employees, direct reports, cross-functional&amp;nbsp;teams, and senior leadership&lt;br&gt;• Well-versed in OSHA regulations and compliance; OSHA certification a plus&lt;br&gt;• Exposure to mechanical, electrical, automation, and refrigeration systems&lt;br&gt;• Ability to read and interpret blueprints, manuals, and schematics&lt;br&gt;• Comfortable working in cold environments (some areas as low as 0°F)&lt;br&gt;• Flexibility to work weekends, holidays, and/or nights&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll get…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Competitive hourly rate, 401K company &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;match that vests immediately upon participation, &amp;amp; team bonus opportunities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Generous PTO and flexible attendance policy&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Comprehensive health and wellness benefits with options at $0 monthly, effective first day of employment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Up to 85% discount on subscriptions to HelloFresh meal plans (HelloFresh, Green Chef, Everyplate, and Factor_)&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Access to Employee Resource Groups that are open to all employees, including those pertaining to BIPOC, women, veterans, parents, and LGBTQ+&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Inclusive, collaborative, and dynamic work environment within a fast-paced, mission-driven company that is disrupting the traditional food supply chain&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This job description is intended to provide a general overview of the responsibilities. However, the Company reserves the right to adjust, modify, or reassign work tasks and responsibilities as needed to meet changing business needs, operational requirements, or other factors.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Texas Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$103,950&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$126,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Newark, NJ Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$119,700&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$145,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Associate Director for Lifecycle, CC Outbound, owns the outbound call center channel strategy and performance for millions of former customers across all 17 of our international markets and all our brands. We are looking for a CRM expert, who is interested in running strategy for Call Center, with a high level of autonomy and agility. You will own the strategic development, performance and strategic innovations for this channel, working closely with the Call Center Operations team. Your scope includes steering performance and managing budgets, implementing strategies that will unlock a better customer experience, under consideration of country-specific idiosyncrasies. It also means developing this channel into one of our prime sources of insight to customer sentiment and inspiration for product improvements at scale (e.g., through the use of AI tools). Moreover, you will own the performance of this channel, which includes setting targets together with our local market CMOs and day-to-day steering of conversions, cost and ROI together with our VP of customer care and his operations managers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you want to own a critical channel for one of our most valuable customer groups and develop a strong muscle in driving CRM strategy and execution, we want to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Above all, we are looking for people who will &lt;strong&gt;make HelloFresh better.&lt;/strong&gt; We believe there are many different ways of developing skills and we love diverse experiences! So even if you don’t “tick all the boxes” but think you’d thrive in this role, we would really like to learn more about you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CRM Strategy Development:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement annual strategic plans for Call Centre Outbound initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the CC Outbound for the full customer lifecycle, from leads to reactivation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with CC Operations, cross-functional teams, local markets and international marketing leadership to align strategies with overall business goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personalization of Customer Interaction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with L&amp;amp;D, Brand and local teams to enrich the training for agents, adding the local context, address the customer needs and have the best pitch for the customer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test personalized offers for customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize AI tools to improve customer interactions and call content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Call Centre Outbound Campaign Management:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and execute outbound communication campaigns. Provide guidance on campaign targeting, messaging, incentives and timing to maximize conversion rates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and steer campaign performance, maximizing ROI and effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure all outbound communication activities comply with relevant regulations and internal expectations (e.g., via quality assurance measures)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data Analysis and Tech Tooling:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage data analysis to identify, test and evaluate impactful reactivation strategies and improvement opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and implement CRM tools to enhance the efficiency and effectiveness of outbound initiatives, coordinating with Call Center Operations and CommsTech.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in and a passion for delivering excellent and effective customer experiences (e.g., working in CRM/Lifecycle Marketing, campaign management, Product, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal skills with an ability to influence and motivate people at all levels within international environments and across a broad variety of job functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ownership mentality and drive to deliver results, including experience with prioritizing for highest impact and managing trade-off decisions in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills and the ability to derive actionable insights from data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ideally hands-on experience working with or in Call Centres&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ideally experience in Experimentation/Testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Modern and comfortable working space with great co-workers in Berlin-Kreuzberg&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discount for HelloFresh boxes and Convini products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Development possibilities along with internal trainings and a yearly Learning &amp;amp; Development budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours including Work From Home/Work from Abroad/Sabbatical Policy, as well as a home office set up budget&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive Onboarding and Buddy Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Social events including team events, Friday beers, company runs, book club, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discounted fitness offers with our Urban Sports Club and John Reed partners and yoga classes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Well-being initiatives in cooperation with Headspace and Spill&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Childcare and company pension scheme benefit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly transportation budget via NAVIT&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Associate Director of Continuous Improvement, Ingredient Quality&amp;nbsp; (North America)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a high-impact leader to bridge the gap between Quality data and Operational execution. This role is designed for a proven, data-driven continuous improvement leader who uses analytics, trends, and structured problem-solving to identify systemic opportunities and deliver measurable results. You have the ability to turn data into scalable operational improvement. This is not a &quot;desk job.&quot; As the Associate Director of Ingredient Excellence &amp;amp; CI, you will be the chief architect and project owner for North American quality standards. You will be responsible for identifying systemic failures and then leading the development and implementation of solutions through our entire supply chain, from suppliers through our operations and right to our customers&#39; doorstep. You are successful only when the metrics move, which requires staying with a project from the initial data deep-dive through to final staff training and process adoption.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Will...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Implementation Lifecycle: Lead the end-to-end development and execution of our ingredient quality error governance. You don’t do band-aid fixes, and you are able to sort signals from noise. You don&#39;t just identify the root cause; you partner with all stakeholders to re-engineer the process and stay on-site until the defect rate drops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect the NA Meal Kit Quality Program: Develop a unified quality focus strategy for our North American network. This involves creating the standards, building the systems &amp;amp; process, and setting up the automated tracking of the execution to ensure consistency across all sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn Data into Action: Use KPIs, trend analysis, and performance data to identify systemic gaps and prioritize the highest-impact improvement opportunities across the network. Translate insights into scalable solutions and measure results to ensure improvements are sustained.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive Operational Accountability: Act as the &quot;boots on the ground&quot; leader who translates quality KPIs into actionable SOPs for our Distribution Centers. You will manage the process implementation to ensure new quality initiatives are adopted, sustained, and reflected in the data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Quality Reporting: Own the North American quality reporting suite. You will evolve our real-time data capabilities to provide the business with predictive insights rather than just post-mortem reports. Use reporting not simply to describe performance, but to identify trends, uncover root causes, prioritize action, and measure business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-Functional Leadership: Serve as the primary quality liaison for Product, Procurement, Operations and Logistics. If they are hearing about problems, you are their first call to help fix it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuous Improvement Mentality: Apply Lean or Six Sigma methodologies to eliminate waste and reduce ingredient damage, directly impacting the bottom line. Lead structured improvement initiatives across multiple sites and translate successful solutions into scalable network standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and Mentor a High-Performance Team: Recruit, train, coach, and manage a team of quality professionals and continuous improvement specialists across North America, fostering a culture of accountability, data-driven decision-making, and excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive Organizational Change: Champion quality-first thinking throughout the organization, influencing leaders and inspiring team members at all levels to adopt new processes and standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Are...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-Driven: You naturally start with the data. You can identify patterns and trends, distinguish symptoms from systemic problems, and turn insights into measurable operational improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Continuous Improvement Leader: You have a demonstrated track record of solving complex problems, improving processes, and scaling successful solutions across sites, functions, or business units.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An Operator at Heart: You understand that a quality program is only as good as the operator’s ability to execute it. You enjoy being on the ground, walking the lines, and solving problems in real-time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A &quot;Finisher&quot;: You have a proven track record of seeing complex projects through to completion. You don&#39;t &quot;throw ideas over the fence&quot;; you jump the fence and help build the solution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic &amp;amp; Tactical: You can present a 3-year quality roadmap to a boardroom in the morning and troubleshoot a conveyor belt/packaging interface with a floor lead in the afternoon.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influential: You can convince Ops leaders to change their processes by proving that higher quality standards lead to higher efficiency and lower costs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Talent Developer: You are a dedicated mentor who takes pride in developing the next generation of quality and operational leaders, providing clear career paths and constructive feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An Influential Communicator: You effectively communicate complex quality initiatives, process changes, and performance results to diverse audiences, from associates in our sites to execs in a meeting room.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At a Minimum, You Have...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience: 8+ years in Continuous Improvement, Operational Excellence, Quality, Supply Chain, or related operational disciplines, with demonstrated experience using data to drive measurable improvements across complex operations. You have a history of managing teams and large-scale projects in a high-volume manufacturing or logistics environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education: Bachelor’s Degree in Food Science, Supply Chain, Engineering, Business, Analytics, or a related discipline. (Lean Six Sigma Green/Black Belt highly preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuous Improvement: Demonstrated experience using Lean, Six Sigma, DMAIC, Kaizen, RCA, or similar structured problem-solving methodologies to deliver measurable results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data &amp;amp; Analytics: Demonstrated ability to analyze KPIs and performance trends, identify systemic gaps, develop actionable insights, and measure the impact of implemented solutions. Experience with data visualization tools such as Tableau or Power BI strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quality/Food: Experience within food manufacturing, distribution, supply chain, quality, or another complex operational environment preferred.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel: Ability to travel up to 25% to North American Distribution Centers. This role requires a physical presence to ensure process implementation is successful.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Newark, NJ Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$140,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$170,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Based in our Chippendale head office in Sydney and reporting to our Director of IT, you will lead the evolution of our APAC IT team from a traditional service desk into a high-performing, globally integrated IT operations hub. Covering HelloConnect Philippines (1,600+ staff across three sites), YouFoodz, BeCool Logistics, and HelloFresh ANZ, this is one of the most dynamic and operationally complex IT leadership roles in the HelloFresh Group.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this position, you will connect regional teams with global leadership, turning big-picture strategy into clear local results, preventing operational silos, and building an IT function ready to scale. As Associate Director, you will act as a trusted advisor to senior executives, shape global IT strategy, and champion IT Operations best practices across the APAC region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define &amp;amp; Own Regional Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Shape and execute the APAC IT strategy across all entities, balancing speed, scope, and quality to seamlessly integrate the region into the global HelloFresh ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead &amp;amp; Master Asynchronous Work:&lt;/strong&gt; Guide a distributed team across Australia, New Zealand, and the Philippines while syncing with Berlin and Toronto. You write clear direction and document key decisions, empowering time-zone-agnostic execution where real-time overlap is optimized and asynchronous is the default.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Evolve Regional Operations:&lt;/strong&gt; Transform a service-desk model into a specialized IT Operations framework, building deep domain expertise so local teams can operate autonomously without constant escalation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner with Executive Stakeholders:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as the trusted IT advisor to APAC business leadership, translating complex technical trade-offs into clear, high-level business recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive SLAs, Compliance &amp;amp; Audits:&lt;/strong&gt; Govern regional performance using Jira Service Management insights, maintaining a robust audit posture and keeping global IT leadership informed on key metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Champion AI Innovation:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead by example with AI tools, actively embedding AI-driven workflows across the team as a core operational standard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optimize Finance &amp;amp; Influence Global Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Maximize regional ROI through smart vendor negotiations, tooling consolidation, and infrastructure streamlining, while representing APAC as a key contributor to global IT strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have/are…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Async-First Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven ability to manage across major time-zone gaps (e.g., aligning Manila with different hemispheres) using clear written communication and structure over constant calls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;APAC Senior Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience at the Associate Director level (or equivalent), with direct accountability for multi-country IT strategy, portfolio ownership, and service delivery across APAC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Philippines &amp;amp; BPO Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience leading or partnering with IT operations in a Philippines-based BPO or shared-services environment—navigating regulatory requirements, multi-site logistics, and remote team management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Stakeholder Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Track record of advising C-suite stakeholders, balancing competing interests, and simplifying complex IT trade-offs into clear decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Distributed Team Building:&lt;/strong&gt; Expertise in leading cross-cultural teams across borders, focusing on performance calibration, coaching, and retention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Adoption:&lt;/strong&gt; Practical experience integrating AI tools into your personal workflows and embedding AI-driven practices within your team to boost efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial &amp;amp; Governance Savvy:&lt;/strong&gt; Skilled in cost optimization via vendor negotiations and tool consolidation. Familiarity with cybersecurity frameworks and BPO regulatory environments is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll get in return…&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The chance to have a significant impact in a leading global food technology company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working arrangements&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Egoless environment, constant learning with room for personal growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free access to Headspace&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Internal learning &amp;amp; development&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A diverse and vibrant international environment, with offices in 18 countries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company discount - 70% off HelloFresh &amp;amp; 40% off Youfoodz&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Start Date: &lt;/strong&gt;Immediately available - Can wait a notice period&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Duration: &lt;/strong&gt;Permanent full time role. You must have the right to work full-time in Australia/New Zealand&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: &lt;/strong&gt;Chippendale Head Office- hybrid working environment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary: &lt;/strong&gt;Competitive salary &amp;amp; employee benefits&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;(( #LI-Hybrid))&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Associate Maintenance Manager&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Come see what’s cookin’ at Factor!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Factor, we aim to revolutionize the way we eat by making it more convenient and exciting to cook meals from scratch. We have offices all around the world and deliver delicious meals to millions of people.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are the industry leader in meal-kit subscription services and we’re growing all the time. We have distinct meal-kit services that cater to everyone with the most menu variety in the market, which allows us to reach an incredibly wide population of people.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team is diverse, high-performing, and international, and our work environment is an inspiring space where you can thrive as a result.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Snapshot&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Associate Maintenance Manager, you will oversee the maintenance and reliability for your assigned building or shift.&amp;nbsp; You will take a hands-on approach to leadership, effectively engaging, motivating, and coaching team members. Partnering with the M&amp;amp;RE senior leadership team, you will support and deliver the facilities maintenance roadmap and set the standard for operational efficiency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;You will...&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee maintenance related processes including maintenance of automation and manufacturing equipment, electrical, refrigeration, building, grounds, and overall upkeep of a building&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Motivate, engage, coach, and inspire a team of technicians, creating a positive team dynamic that encourages all employees to provide feedback and drive change from within&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage outside vendors and facilitate planned and unplanned repairs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that maintenance regulations are followed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a current list of contractors to ensure that all emergency repairs are handled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify problems and brainstorm improvement ideas for the fulfillment center&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;You are…&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer Centric: You are passionate about delivering on commitments to your customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bold: you have passion and grit; you&#39;re not afraid to give feedback to your team and your manager&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agile: you roll with the punches and don’t get overwhelmed easily, you adapt quickly to change and know how to deliver results in a fast-paced, autonomous environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Decisive: You realize when making a decision is as important as the time it takes to make that decision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Problem-solver: you understand there is not a one-size-fits-all approach when problem-solving; you think outside the box and enjoy grinding away at issues to find a solution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;You have…&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;0 to 2+ years’ experience managing facilities maintenance/operations and reliability within the&amp;nbsp;Food/Beverage/Perishables/Distribution industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s Degree preferred; high school diploma or GED required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in spending most of your time on the shop floor and working directly with all levels of staff&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High level of integrity and ethics with excellent follow-through&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Aware of OSHA regulations and compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to read and interpret blueprints, manuals, and schematics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to mechanical, electrical, automation and refrigeration systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in cold environments with some areas of facility at 40F&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excitement for working in a start-up environment with a high level of ambiguity and change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective communicator for employees, direct reports, cross-functional teams, and senior leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility to work weekends, holidays and/or nights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;You’ll get…&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary &amp;amp; 401K company match that vests immediately upon participation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid parental leave (16 weeks)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous PTO policy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Day one benefit coverage for health/dental/vision ($0 monthly premium and other flexible health plans)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;75% discount on your subscription to HelloFresh, as well as other product initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Snacks, coffee &amp;amp; catered meals&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company sponsored outings &amp;amp; Employee Resource Groups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative, dynamic work environment within a fast-paced, mission-driven company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;em&gt;Your decision to redact this information will not adversely affect the consideration of your application. We evaluate all candidates based on their skills, qualifications, and experience. Please be aware that should you receive a conditional offer of employment, we may be required to request this information for legally permissible purposes, such as verifying eligibility for employment or for benefits administration and background checks.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;S&#39;more about the team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a driven and analytical Supply Chain Enablement Associate Manager to support the transformation of our ingredients and packaging inbound supply chain. Reporting to the Associate Director, Supply Chain Enablement, you will lead standalone supply chain process and technology improvement workstreams end-to-end — turning operational signals into data-driven cases and delivering measurable impact. As a part of the Procurement team, you will develop deep expertise in our processes, data, and technology, building the analytical foundation that drives continuous improvement across our E2E supply chain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will succeed in this role by combining structured analytical thinking, effective cross-functional collaboration, and strong project management skills to independently own and deliver workstreams from problem definition through implementation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lettuce share what this role will be responsible for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead standalone supply chain process and technology improvement workstreams end-to-end, from opportunity identification and root cause analysis through implementation and adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build data-driven analytical cases — quantify opportunity size and impact, assess root causes, and make clear recommendations to fix, standardize, or escalate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run deep current- and future-state process mapping to isolate root causes; independently lead root cause and corrective action (RCCA) on workstream-level problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional stakeholders across the organization (including teams from procurement, planning, logistics, technology, data, fulfillment operations, and finance) to align on solutions and drive workstream-level change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary mentor and quality gate for offshore resources within your workstream — vetting new workstreams, defining execution plans, auditing quality, and managing SLA variances&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to our source-to-pay technology and process knowledge; support master data and technology initiatives within your workstream scope&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and improve standard operating procedures and documentation for workstream processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage project plans, Jira workflows, and timelines; provide stakeholder updates and collaborate with our data team to track KPIs and report on progress&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All other duties as assigned&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sound a-peeling? Here&#39;s what we&#39;re looking for:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s and/or Graduate degree in Business Management, Supply Chain Management, Engineering, or equivalent field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of relevant consulting or industry experience with logistics, supply chain management, operations, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to build analytical cases — quantifying impact, sizing opportunities, and translating data into clear, actionable recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading process improvement projects end-to-end, including stakeholder alignment, change communication, and post-implementation tracking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of Lean methodologies and root cause analysis tools (e.g., 5 Whys, Variable Tree Analysis); Lean Six Sigma Green Belt certification is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in data analysis and visualization tools (e.g., Google Sheets, Tableau, Looker); ability to build or contribute to reporting dashboards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subject matter knowledge in one or more of: procure-to-pay, source-to-pay, process mapping, spend analysis, or performance metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to collaborate across cross-functional teams and engage stakeholders at multiple levels of the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear and structured communication skills, with the ability to synthesize complex information and present recommendations to cross-functional audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating in a fast-paced, ambiguous environment with the ability to self-direct a workstream with limited guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
