&lt;li&gt;Inspect inbound ingredients against specifications, log results, and log tickets promptly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promptly escalate quality or safety issues and collaborate with partner teams for fast resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete quarterly inspection refresher trainings to stay up to date.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support dock receiving with HACCP reviews, allergen labeling checks, and handling verifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure receiving operational practices comply fully with company standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Warehouse teams to uphold safe ingredient handling practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct inspected shipments smoothly to designated work areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform continuous quality checks on produce, dairy, protein, and grocery items throughout processing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct mandatory audits, sanitation swabs, temperature checks, and expiration verifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strictly adhere to and enforce all safety, GMP, and SQF guidelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As Assigned;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Audit line setups, completed kits, and packaging processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Alert leadership to errors, assist in corrective actions, and halt production lines for critical non-conformances.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track discarded items and evaluate ingredients for potential recovery and reuse.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
