&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Copywriter, Global Creative Studio (m/f/x)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Brand Marketing · Berlin or Warsaw&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At HelloFresh Group, our mission is to change the way people eat forever. Since our 2011 founding in Berlin, we&#39;ve become the global market leader in the meal kit sector, inspiring millions of home cooks and food lovers every week. Our portfolio spans eight brands across 16 markets, from HelloFresh and Factor to Good Chop and Pets Table.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE JOB&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you love making words work hard, this might be your job.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HelloFresh Group is looking for a Lead Copywriter to join our Creative Studio and help drive copy quality across our demand generation engine. You&#39;ll work across the full funnel and across every channel that matters (TV, OOH, paid social, display, CRM, YouTube) with a particular focus on mid-funnel, paid social creative that stops thumbs and starts conversations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on writing role, creating everything from campaign headlines to push notifications, from social hooks to CRM journeys. You&#39;ll also bring the strategic thinking to help shape how eight global brands communicate across sixteen markets, and the collaborative instinct to consult with local teams, advise channel owners, and help more junior staffers write better.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Crucially, you will help build, train, and socialize AI tools (particularly on Claude and Gemini) to create and maintain&amp;nbsp; a broad creative toolkit. You will use these tools to generate, iterate, and localize content, but you will be the creative brain behind all LLM work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is based in Berlin or Warsaw. Berlin-based employees have required attendance three days per week (Monday to Wednesday) at our Creative Studio in Moabit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write sharp, on-brand copy across the full funnel and all major channels (paid social, display, CRM, YouTube, TV, and OOH), with a particular emphasis on mid-funnel paid social creative.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring big-picture strategic thinking to campaign briefs and creative concepts, while staying just as comfortable writing a single subject line or a two-second video hook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consult with local market copywriting teams across sixteen markets, offering guidance, feedback, and creative direction that keeps their work on-brand and high-quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI tools (especially Claude and Gemini) as part of your creative workflow: for ideation, iteration, and developing prompt frameworks and localization pipelines that improve quality and efficiency at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise channel owners and marketing stakeholders on copy strategy, messaging hierarchy, and how to make creative work harder at every touchpoint.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape, evolve, and maintain tone of voice and messaging guidelines across eight brands, ensuring they’re clear and practical enough to use at local and global levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with designers, videographers, motion designers, and performance marketers to bring creative ideas to life and optimize them for conversion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interpret performance data to understand what&#39;s working, and use those insights to improve briefs, iterate on copy, and sharpen your craft.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rigorously proofread copy. Zero typos, zero grammatical errors, no exceptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage content flows via Google Suite, Airtable, and Jira so copy moves efficiently from brief to stakeholders to market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHO WE ARE LOOKING FOR&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A full-time copywriter based in, or willing to relocate to, Berlin or Warsaw.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS/MS from a top-tier university in Communications, Marketing, Creative Writing, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of copywriting or communications experience, ideally spanning both agency and in-house environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of high-impact, English-language copy across major digital channels, especially paid social, display, CRM, email, and YouTube.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strategic thinker who can see the big picture across brands and markets, but who is equally happy polishing a push notification or reworking a subject line.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An experienced AI worker, using LLMs as part of a creative process to generate, refine, and localize copy more effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A natural collaborator who can consult with and advise local teams and channel owners—someone who leads through the quality of their thinking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working within brand and tone guidelines, and experienced enough to know when to push the boundaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to write across multiple projects, brands, markets, and tones simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A curiosity about audiences and the ability to interpret performance data to refine copy strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with localization and machine translation workflows is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agency experience, particularly at a social media-focused or digital agency, is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working for food or tech brands is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of German, French, Swedish, Norwegian, Danish, or Dutch is a plus.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ARE YOU UP FOR THE CHALLENGE?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To apply, please complete the application and send us a portfolio that shows your range: performance-driven digital copy, campaign thinking across brands or markets, and any examples of how you&#39;ve worked smarter—whether that&#39;s AI-assisted workflows, localization processes, or something else entirely.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re excited to see what you bring to the team.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HelloFresh is seeking a Lead Equity &amp;amp; Incentives Compensation Partner to drive the strategy and execution of our global equity programs, short- and long-term incentive plans, executive compensation, and rewards governance framework. This is a senior individual contributor role for someone who has been deep in the mechanics of compensation in a high-growth technology company and is now ready to own a portfolio that spans program design, governance, and cross-functional influence. You will play a foundational role in defining our global rewards strategy and structuring defensible compensation frameworks.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Global Director, Compensation Strategy, you will serve as the subject matter expert across equity, incentives, and executive pay - working at the intersection of people, finance, legal, and the business. This role is central to building scalable, market-competitive compensation programs that support HelloFresh&#39;s continued growth across global markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity Program Design &amp;amp; Execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Program Ownership: Lead the design, administration, and continuous improvement of HelloFresh&#39;s global equity programs - including RSUs, performance shares, and any new equity vehicles - ensuring they are competitive, compliant, and well-understood by employees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Platform &amp;amp; Data Integrity: Serve as the operational lead for the equity compensation platform, ensuring accurate data bridges between Workday, Payroll, and external equity administration tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity Education: Develop scalable education materials - guides, FAQs, webinars - that help employees across all markets understand their equity awards and the broader compensation philosophy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Incentive&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Plans &amp;amp; Variable Pay&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;STI &amp;amp; LTI Design: Lead the design and annual refresh of short-term and long-term incentive structures, including corporate bonus plans, sales incentive frameworks, and performance-based equity programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan Modelling: Build and maintain incentive compensation models to evaluate cost, dilution, payout scenarios, and competitive positioning; translate model outputs into clear recommendations for senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Goal-Setting &amp;amp; Calibration: Partner with Finance and HR Business Partners during the annual goal-setting cycle to ensure incentive metrics are appropriately rigorous, measurable, and aligned to business priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pay Mix Analysis: Conduct ongoing analysis of total compensation pay mix across roles, levels, and geographies to identify gaps and recommend design adjustments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Executive Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;C-Suite Support: Support executive compensation reviews, including benchmarking for C-suite and director-level roles, peer group analysis, and preparation of materials for Compensation Committee review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Benchmarking &amp;amp; Market Data: Manage relationships with compensation survey vendors; lead annual and ad-hoc benchmarking exercises to keep HelloFresh&#39;s executive pay competitive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Offer Construction: Partner with Talent Acquisition and senior HR leadership to structure competitive offers for executive hires, including equity, sign-on, and ongoing compensation considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Disclosure &amp;amp; Reporting: Support preparation of executive compensation disclosures and Compensation Committee materials, ensuring accuracy and regulatory compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Rewards Governance &amp;amp; Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Governance Framework: Develop and maintain HelloFresh&#39;s global compensation governance framework — including salary band structures, job architecture, and pay approval workflows — ensuring consistency, fairness, and auditability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regulatory Compliance: Ensure all compensation programs comply with applicable securities law, tax regulations, and reporting requirements across jurisdictions (DE, US, UK, and others); lead preparation for the EU Pay Transparency Directive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pay Equity: Design and execute regular pay equity analyses across gender, ethnicity, and tenure; surface findings and drive remediation plans in partnership with HR leadership and Legal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SOX &amp;amp; Audit Support: Maintain rigorous controls and documentation for equity and incentive programs to support internal and external audit requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process Improvement: Identify and implement opportunities to automate and streamline compensation operations, including tooling, workflows, and AI-assisted analytics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Strategic Partnership &amp;amp; Program Building&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-Functional Influence: Act as the compensation expert for HR Business Partners, Finance, and Legal — providing timely, data-driven guidance on compensation decisions across the employee lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;M&amp;amp;A and Expansion: Support compensation due diligence and integration work for acquisitions and new market entries, ensuring programs can scale with the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stakeholder Communication: Translate complex compensation concepts into clear narratives for senior leaders, the Compensation Committee, and employees at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team Mentorship: Provide guidance and mentorship to more members of the compensation team, including the Senior Equity Compensation Analyst.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience: &lt;/strong&gt;8+ years of progressive compensation experience, with at least 4 years focused on equity, incentives, or executive compensation in a high-growth global technology or e-commerce company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Program Builder: &lt;/strong&gt;Demonstrated track record of designing and scaling compensation programs from the ground up — not just administering inherited ones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Depth: &lt;/strong&gt;Strong command of equity mechanics (RSUs, options, performance shares), incentive plan design, and executive pay practices. Familiarity with SOX, EU Pay Transparency, and multi-jurisdictional compliance requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical Rigour: &lt;/strong&gt;Expert-level proficiency in financial modelling and data analysis (Excel/Google Sheets required; SQL, Python, or BI tools a plus). Comfortable building models that inform multi-million dollar decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Governance Mindset: &lt;/strong&gt;Experience developing or maintaining global compensation governance frameworks, job architectures, and pay equity programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Influence: &lt;/strong&gt;Proven ability to work effectively with Finance, Legal, Talent, and senior executives; capable of presenting complex analyses in simple, compelling terms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications: &lt;/strong&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Finance, HR, Economics, or a related field. Certifications such as Certified Compensation Professional (CCP) or Certified Equity Professional (CEP) are highly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adaptability: &lt;/strong&gt;Comfortable operating in ambiguity and navigating rapid change; thrives in a fast-paced, high-ownership environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Elevate your lifestyle! Join one of Europe&#39;s fastest-growing tech powerhouses in a dynamic phase of expansion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Immerse yourself in a diverse global community of 90+ nationalities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy a competitive compensation package that goes beyond the norm, with perks like a HelloFresh- subsidized Pension Scheme, Berlin relocation support, and a Hybrid working model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Elevate your lifestyle with exclusive discounts on your weekly HelloFresh box and office meals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Invest in your growth with an annual learning &amp;amp; development budget, German language learning budget, and access to the HelloFresh Academy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plus, we&#39;ve got your well-being covered with mental health support, transportation perks, and working-parent-friendly benefits. From our 24/7 gym access,wellbeing platforms like Headspace and Spill, to sabbatical leave options, HelloFresh is not just a workplace; it&#39;s a lifestyle of perks and possibilities!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Are you up for the challenge?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Please submit your complete application below including your salary expectations and earliest starting date.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;After submitting an application our team will review this and get back to you within 5 business days.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As a Lead Maintenance Technician, you will assist maintenance management in coordinating and leading work with the maintenance team to maintain and repair conveyance, automation and facilities equipment to support operations uptime and improve reliability of our systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shift: Wednesday to Saturday - 6:00am to 4:30pm&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and educate compliance with all safety, food safety, and security standards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform preventive maintenance and routine inspections on assigned conveyors, automation, robotics and ancillary equipment as needed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform troubleshooting of assigned out of service equipment and correct issues, act as an escalation point for lower level technicians, and escalate to leadership and/or vendors as needed for additional troubleshooting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document all work in the computerized maintenance management system (CMMS) and ticketing systems as appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor all maintenance personnel in developing appropriate skill sets and knowledge of equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead root cause analysis of major downtime events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the maintenance Point of Contact in the absence of the maintenance leader for the site.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist managers in developing training materials and performing training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform administrative functions including inventory management, assigning work, and minor project management as assigned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform building project work as assigned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4-6 years of experience with conveyor, automation, robotics, and/or refrigeration repair and maintenance including mechanical and electrical operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced understanding of machinery and equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic skill level in multiple computer software packages including Microsoft Excel and/or Google Sheets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read and understand basic schematics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to indirectly lead and influence a maintenance team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel as necessary (up to 5%) for business purposes.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High School diploma or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent follow through, judgment, and common sense. &quot;Make it happen&quot; attitude.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Associates degree or equivalent preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with inputs, outputs, and PLC logic systems and ability to troubleshoot these systems preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll get…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive hourly rate, 401K company match that vests immediately upon participation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous PTO and additional sick leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive health and wellness benefits with options at $0 monthly, effective first day of employment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Up to 85% discount on subscriptions to HelloFresh meal plans (HelloFresh, Green Chef, Everyplate, and Factor_) &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to Employee Resource Groups that are open to all employees, including those pertaining to BIPOC, women, veterans, parents, and LGBTQ+&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inclusive, collaborative, and dynamic work environment within a fast-paced, mission-driven company that is disrupting the traditional food supply chain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This job description is intended to provide a general overview of the responsibilities. However, the Company reserves the right to adjust, modify, or reassign work tasks and responsibilities as needed to meet changing business needs, operational requirements, or other factors.&lt;/p&gt;
